//! GENERATED by contract-gen from crates/k2-core/src/contract/catalog.json (rows exposed to `app`).
//! Do not edit: change the catalog, then run `cargo run -p k2-core --bin contract-gen`
//! (prd-zen-user-widgets-v2 UWA11). The freshness tests fail on drift.
//!
//! The App-facing route table (`prd-k2-app-runtime-v1` §5.1, §5.3, AR8,
//! S23): the one list of `/cli/*` routes and sockets an App may reach.
//!
//! Two doors read it:
//! - the browser helper (`k2-daemon --skin-gateway`), forwarding a guest's
//!   session pass from the App's origin ([`HTTP_ALLOWLIST`]);
//! - the App's **gateway link** (`apps::gateway` in k2-daemon), the per-App
//!   listener a walled App calls with its App pass ([`link_allows_http`]).
//!
//! Default deny: a route not listed here is refused at both doors before
//! any handler runs. Every row is a catalog verb exposed to `app`; a route
//! that isn't catalogued can't be listed (and `contract::gen`'s freshness
//! test fails a hand edit).

